   "subject": "Merging several brms objects into one",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><font size=\"2\"><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(36,39,41)\">Suppose I have more than one brms </span><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(36,39,41)\">object obtained by running the same brms </span><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(36,39,41)\">model-fitting function on the same data. Is it possible to merge these </span><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(36,39,41)\">objects into one consolidated brms </span><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(36,39,41)\">object?</span></font><br></span><div><font size=\"2\"><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(36,39,41);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><br></span></font></div><div><font size=\"2\"><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(36,39,41);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">A solution to this problem would help consolidating the output data of brms when the models are fitted on multiple processors on an HPC cluster.</span></font></div><div><font size=\"2\"><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(36,39,41);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><br></span></font></div><div><font size=\"2\"><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(36,39,41);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><br></span></font></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "y8ubSSO0AgAJ",
