   "date": "2018-01-04T16:27:49Z",
   "subject": "Re: [brms-users] Merging several brms objects into one",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>This has not been possible previously. However, I just added a function called &#39;combine_models&#39; to the dev version of brms that should do the job.<br><br></div>You can install the dev version via<br><br><pre><span>if</span> (<span>!</span>require(<span><span>&quot;</span>devtools<span>&quot;</span></span>)) {\r\n  install.packages(<span><span>&quot;</span>devtools<span>&quot;</span></span>)\r\n}\r\n<span>devtools</span><span>::</span>install_github(<span><span>&quot;</span>paul-buerkner/brms<span>&quot;</span></span>, <span>dependencies</span> <span>=</span> <span>TRUE</span>)<br><br></pre></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">2018-01-04 14:23 GMT+01:00 RV <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">r.vo...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span>:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><font size=\"2\"><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(36,39,41)\">Suppose I have more than one brms </span><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(36,39,41)\">object obtained by running the same brms </span><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(36,39,41)\">model-fitting function on the same data. Is it possible to merge these </span><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(36,39,41)\">objects into one consolidated brms </span><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(36,39,41)\">object?</span></font><br></span><div><font size=\"2\"><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(36,39,41);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><br></span></font></div><div><font size=\"2\"><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(36,39,41);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">A solution to this problem would help consolidating the output data of brms when the models are fitted on multiple processors on an HPC cluster.</span></font></div><span><font color=\"#888888\"><div><font size=\"2\"><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(36,39,41);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><br></span></font></div><div><font size=\"2\"><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(36,39,41);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><br></span></font></div></font></span></div></blockquote></div></div>"
